# Zustand stores

Read `docs/STORES_REFERENCE.md` for entrypoints and `docs/ORG_SCOPED_ASYNC_SAFETY.md` for ownership.

- Keep each store in its domain owner; adapt transport DTOs before publishing domain state.
- Use narrow selectors. Derived collection snapshots must retain references when all inputs are unchanged; use existing memoization/selector patterns and stable empty fallbacks.
- Update state immutably. Do not mutate a Map/array in place when subscribers depend on reference changes.
- Workspace keys are UUID/runtime identities, not automatically numeric IDs. Scope durable state and async writes to the current owner.
- Avoid copying a growing map for every catch-up event when an ordered batch can preserve semantics; cursor and cache behavior must remain correct.
- Do not create a store, persist every field, or log every action by template. Keep private data out of diagnostics.
